- Story & Context: Kaelen, the station’s senior operator, stares at the humming electric sitar and admits to his apprentice that the instrument was built from the copper wiring of a decommissioned foghorn. The air in the room tastes of ozone and burnt salt as he confesses that he has been intentionally misdirecting ships to keep the frequency alive. "If the note stays pure, the dark won't claim the hull."
